WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.099
North Korea wouldn’t be that well-known
if it weren't for its nuclear tests, its tyrannical

00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:31.710
and extravagant government and its characteristic
insults on international leaders, especially

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:39.579
those from the United States.

00:00:39.579 --> 00:00:41.470
Comparatively speaking, it’s a rather poor
country.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:47.380
A country that has just over 25 million inhabitants,
no relevant industry or commerce and a strikingly

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.820
low purchasing power.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:58.019
However, North Korea has been, is and will
be a leading player in many international

00:00:58.019 --> 00:01:03.129
forums and summits, due to its constant human
rights violations and its advanced nuclear

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.489
and ballistic program.

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:15.970
The fact is that 2019 was a particularly complicated
year for its dictator, Kim Jong-Un, and 2020

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:21.409
doesn’t look much better.

00:01:21.409 --> 00:01:26.270
Because you see, along with the effects of
international sanctions on imported materials

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:30.850
and products of all kinds, the country is
going through a severe food crisis due to

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:36.270
drought, floods and other circumstances that
have caused crop yields to drop to a 5-year

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.270
low.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:42.280
To give you an idea, food shortages are estimated
to affect almost 40% of North Koreans.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.320
This means that the State cannot guarantee
the minimum nutritional requirements to more

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.180
than 10 million people.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:55.890
So ten million people now depend on international
humanitarian assistance.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:00.310
South Korea, for example, has offered them
50,000 tons of rice to alleviate hunger.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:05.369
However, as we’ve told you before on VisualPolitik,
despite this difficult situation, the North

00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:07.780
Korean economy has been growing for years.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:12.190
Although growth has come in a somewhat strange,
informal, chaotic way, and is largely driven

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:17.260
by the black market, the truth is that North
Korea’s economy has made certain progress

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:20.070
in recent years.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:26.070
We’re talking about an irregular economic
growth, but it’s estimated that, in some

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:29.570
years, it averaged a 5% annual rate.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:32.720
But don’t get excited.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:38.030
We’re talking about growth rates where the
starting point was extreme poverty, and growth

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:43.810
which has only reached certain urban centers.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:49.190
40% of North Koreans living in rural areas
aren’t even guaranteed energy.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:53.959
Growth and the North Korean government’s
investments in particular can only be seen

00:02:53.959 --> 00:02:59.750
in very limited areas such as Pyongyang and
other secondary cities like Wonsan, Sinuiju,

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:06.220
Rason or Samjiyon.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:11.080
In the rest of North Korea, people basically
have to go out to cut the few remaining trees

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.270
in the radically deforested landscape in order
to keep warm in winter.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:25.840
This image, this reality greatly clashes with
the other that is projected.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.760
This is the new Pyongyang that the North Korean
regime is trying to build.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.299
And we aren’t just talking about Pyongyang.

00:03:32.299 --> 00:03:42.370
In recent years they’ve endorsed macro projects
that are no longer focussed only in the capital.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:44.699
Projects which have prompted the international
community to ask:

00:03:44.699 --> 00:03:49.540
Are these the result of the megalomania of
Kim Jong Un, a young dictator who grew up

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.889
studying in private schools in Switzerland
and watching NBA games, or are they signs

00:03:53.889 --> 00:03:55.490
that the government wants to change?

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:59.590
We can’t answer that question, but in this
video, we’re going to tell you about North

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.890
Korea’s main macro projects.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.120
You may be in for a surprise.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:04.120
Let's go!

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.320
By the way, if you want to know where the
North Korean government gets the resources

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:25.110
for all these projects, don’t miss the videos

00:04:25.110 --> 00:05:32.729
that I’ll link in the description.

00:05:32.729 --> 00:05:52.330
(PYONGYANG, FROM STALINIST GRAY TO MULTICOLOR
MEGALOMANIA)

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:58.030
When we think of Pyongyang, many of you may
only think of the husk of that gigantic pyramid-shaped

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:02.919
hotel that cost a bomb to complete.

00:06:02.919 --> 00:06:09.340
A husk that didn’t see a single worker for
more than 15 years.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:14.580
Between 1992 and 2008 construction was completely
paralyzed, simply because the North Korean

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:21.849
government lacked the resources to complete
it.

00:06:21.849 --> 00:06:26.220
First as a result of the fall of the Soviet
Union and then due to the effects of the Arduous

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:32.120
March, a famine that ended the lives of more
than two million people.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:38.169
It’s a building that’s been called one
of the great emblems of the regime, whose

00:06:38.169 --> 00:06:43.610
construction was implemented by Kim Il Sung,
the grandfather of the Kim dynasty, and remained

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:48.680
unfinished throughout Kim Jong Il’s entire
era, and which Kim Jong Un covered with glass

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.029
and a giant LED screen.

00:06:52.029 --> 00:06:55.990
What’s inside, nobody can tell.

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:59.349
As for a hotel, a real hotel, it doesn’t
look like one.

00:06:59.349 --> 00:07:03.729
Since its completion in 2016, not a single
guest has been seen to enter.

00:07:03.729 --> 00:07:08.629
In other words, we’re looking at a first-class
prop.

00:07:08.629 --> 00:07:15.550
But don’t think that this is a useless microproject,
not at all.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:24.440
Wait to see what has been erected in Pyongyang
in recent years, and what’s to come.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:27.340
For example, there’s the Mirae street of
scientists.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:28.900
Mirae means “future” in Korean.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.770
It’s a street full of residential skyscrapers,
shops and restaurants serving Korean and International

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:34.770
food.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:38.129
This avenue was opened as a prize for the
nuclear program’s scientists, and for university

00:07:38.129 --> 00:07:40.550
professors who were in step with the regime.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:44.659
It has car access control, which makes it
a kind of gated neighborhood.

00:07:44.659 --> 00:07:45.659
Social classes?

00:07:45.659 --> 00:07:48.939
Who said social classes?

00:07:48.939 --> 00:07:55.699
And that’s not all, the most recent one,
in Ryomyong Avenue, was inaugurated in April

00:07:55.699 --> 00:08:01.509
2017, and has almost 20 residential skyscrapers,
many of them painted with blue and turquoise

00:08:01.509 --> 00:08:06.759
and decorated with lots of tiles, to imitate
the color of the glass of modern skyscrapers

00:08:06.759 --> 00:08:11.180
in neighbouring South Korea and China.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:17.030
Now, what exactly is the real objective of
these projects?

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:22.129
Well... here the goal is twofold: A local
objective and an international one.

00:08:22.129 --> 00:08:31.029
The local goal was the message that Kim Jong
Un wanted to transmit to the North Korean

00:08:31.029 --> 00:08:33.750
power core in his early years as a leader.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:38.650
Kim wanted to convey the idea that even though
he was young, he would be the one to modernize,

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:42.289
develop and transform the country, no matter
what happened outside.

00:08:42.289 --> 00:08:46.110
And in a way, this was the best news for the
international community: an apparent change

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.110
of spirit.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:51.760
Although the truth is that wasting resources
on such sterile projects doesn’t look like

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.230
the best way to achieve it.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:09:01.620
And on the other hand, Kim builds all these
works, which he can’t afford, to convey

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:03.650
a message to the world.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:04.650
Something like:

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:09.400
Hey, “You can throw all the sanctions you
want at me, Juche socialism is strong and

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.400
will resist.”

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:17.750
Because that’s precisely the message that
holds Kim in power, his chest beat before

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:18.750
the West.

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:21.800
Even if he’s only pretending to be something
he isn’t.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:27.850
In any case, what seems clear is that this
kind of golden veneer will continue for a

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:29.280
while for Pyongyang.

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:33.790
Kim Jong Un just presented a new macro project
in 2019, to completely change the neighborhood

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.760
that surrounds the ghost hotel.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:41.890
(AUDIO: KCTV reveals large-scale plans for
district surrounding iconic Ryugyong Hotel

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:42.890
- NK News)

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:44.210
But just a second.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:48.430
So far, we’ve only talked about the capital
but... what’s happening outside Pyongyang?

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:52.760
Is Kim also promoting these types of projects
outside the flashy capital?

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:57.750
The answer is yes, he is.

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:03.720
In fact, the most outlandish projects are
being carried out beyond the capital.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:09.700
In particular Samjiyon and the Kalma Peninsula,
in the city of Wonsan.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:17.880
But, of course, I know you’re thinking:
Simon, who’s ever heard of those places?

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.400
Well, until now they had no relevance whatsoever.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:25.720
But, Kim, as a good kid who was educated in
Switzerland, wanted to have his own version

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:30.030
of a European-style ski resort, as well as
his own summer vacation town.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:33.870
And that’s exactly what he’s making.

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:36.960
The objective?

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.610
Supposedly to flood his country with tourism.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:45.250
In 2018, North Korea received a record number
of visitors: 1.2 million Chinese tourists,

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:47.810
50% more than in 2017.

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:51.250
And along with them, the odd handful of tourists
from other nationalities.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:57.200
Of course, all duly accompanied by guides
who control their movements at all times.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:04.430
But yes, tourism fever seems to be reaching
even as far as North Korea.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:09.190
Would you like to know more about Kim's ultimate
commitment to gain the foreign currency he

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:11.970
direly needs after all the international sanctions?

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:19.910
Well, listen up.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:29.700
(TWO NEW CITIES FOR WINTER AND SUMMER)

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:35.620
To turn North Korea into something like the
Thailand of Northeast Asia, Kim Jong Un is

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:39.820
spending a lot of money – a lot, considering
the country’s true economic standing, – to

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:41.780
create tourist complexes.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:47.850
We can see the two greatest examples in Samjiyon
and Kalma.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:54.880
Samjiyon is a town located at the foot of
Mount Paektu, which according to Korean tradition

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:56.900
is the place where Korea was founded.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:12:01.550
And also where, according to North Korean
propaganda cartoons, Kim Jong Il was born,

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:08.740
you know while birds sang and a bright rainbow
danced on the horizon.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:14.050
The fact is that, today this region is better
known for being one of the most beautiful

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:18.910
natural places in the country and for having
fantastic conditions for winter sports.

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:24.120
And that’s precisely where Kim Jong Un decided
to build his miniature Switzerland.

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:31.740
Therefore, he ordered the entire town to be
demolished to build a new one with a large

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:36.820
hotel, shops, apartment blocks and houses
with colored roofs, to house 4,000 families,

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:41.130
380 public and industrial buildings and, of
course, a few ski slopes.

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:42.950
All this was built in a year and a half.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:49.820
Of course, when we look behind the curtains,
the story isn’t as impressive.

00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:56.380
To complete the build, the regime employed
semi-slave labor and even the army itself.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:13:00.410
Workers were mobilized from forced labor camps,
and electricity had to be redirected from

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:03.130
the surrounding towns, leaving the towns without
power.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:07.010
And all this in order to finish as planned,
in the first quarter of 2020, to be able to

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.470
take advantage of that year's winter campaign.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:14.050
Because if there’s one thing Kim needs,
it's cash.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:18.260
Dollars, euros, yen, yuan...

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:19.310
Money!

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:24.700
Perhaps, with a bit of luck, one or two Chinese
tourists will go down his ski slopes and stay

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.150
in one of his soulless accommodations.

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:32.570
Anyway, Samjiyon has been sold by the regime
as “the socialist utopia”, the demonstration

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:34.890
that the regime can create a winter paradise.

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:39.520
However, Martha Thorne, executive director
of the prestigious Pritzker Architecture Prize,

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:40.820
doesn’t see it that way.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:41.820
Check this out.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.360
(“It's just a simple ski resort.

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:45.590
It doesn't reflect any new ways of living.

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.810
It puts little emphasis on urban quality and
public land use.

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:52.480
And it doesn't project spaces where people
can develop a full life.”

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.690
Martha Thorne, executive director of the Prtizker
Prize)

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:59.370
But well beyond these debates about urban
planning and the fact that it seems economically

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:04.570
unfeasible, Samjiyon is currently one of the
best places in the worst place on the planet.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:09.760
The question now is whether they’ll be able
to reproduce this in Kalma, in the city of

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:10.760
Wonsan.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:13.820
What is being built there is almost the opposite
of the snowy Samjiyon.

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:21.340
We’re talking about a true summer vacation
city.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:25.190
From end to end, it consists of almost five
kilometers of buildings that are all currently

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:26.230
under construction.

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:31.270
All this with a newly remodeled airport and
a beautiful and shiny terminal, to which nobody

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:32.270
flies.

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:37.830
Kim Jong Un wants it to be the Cancun of the
East Sea, the North Korean Miami, the Communist

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:39.780
Benidorm.

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:47.630
The project’s magnitude makes it perhaps
the most expensively unrestrained project

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:50.340
of the last decade for impoverished North
Korea.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:54.730
We’re talking about 12 hotels, 2 shopping
centers, 26 commercial buildings, cinemas,

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:59.300
an exhibition palace, an arcade game building,
an indoor water park, an ice-skating rink,

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:05.130
a restaurant complex and more than 48 mansions
and 200 Luxury chalets to lure the tourist

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.130
dollar.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:13.312
All this in a country that’s closed to the
world and anchored in extreme poverty, where

00:15:13.312 --> 00:15:18.260
a large part of the population has trouble
even getting the minimum nutrients they need

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:21.760
to live.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:28.160
Obviously, most North Koreans won’t be able
to enjoy this.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:32.500
The country's elites, senior officials and
perhaps some tourists may use these services.

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:40.380
But the others... obviously won’t.

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:44.570
And it doesn’t stop there, because in addition
to Pyongyang, Samjiyon and Wonsan, other cities

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:50.410
like Sinuiju, on the border with China, are
also seeing a certain real estate boom.

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:58.020
For example, there’s the construction of
this sun-shaped hotel in the Kangmun district.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:01.860
It’s designed to house businessmen once
the Sinuiju Special Economic Zone between

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.010
North Korea and China is activated.

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:11.990
Right now that zone is crippled by international
sanctions.

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:16.870
Kim's idea is to reform the entire riverfront
of the Yalu River, to not only exploit the

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:21.380
growing economic activity that is brewing
in this area thanks to trade with China and

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:25.550
the black market – in which the government
itself participates – but also to make the

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:30.860
view from the other side, where the prosperous
Chinese city of Dangdong is located, a picture

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:33.430
of development and prosperity.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:41.280
Now that you’re familiar with North Korea’s
main macro projects, there’s something we

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:42.640
really need to clarify.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:45.160
All these projects may look like examples
of development...

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:48.720
But the reality is very different.

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:55.630
In most cases, these types of projects simply
end up empty, because there are no people

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:58.760
to attend or customers to pay for anything….

00:16:58.760 --> 00:16:59.760
Ghost towns.

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:04.059
If he doesn’t radically open up to the world,
Kim Jong Un will be wasting hundreds of millions

00:17:04.059 --> 00:17:08.820
of dollars, which could be used for many more
necessary things, such as improving the country's

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:10.319
poor infrastructure.

00:17:10.319 --> 00:17:20.329
To give you an idea, of the more than 25,500
kilometers of roads that the country has,

00:17:20.329 --> 00:17:21.640
only 800 are paved.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:27.920
That’s barely 3%.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:32.160
These resources could also be spent on dams,
pipelines and dikes to avoid flooding when

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:36.340
it rains heavily, and also to collect water
reserves to prevent recurrent droughts and

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:39.090
therefore food shortages.

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:47.259
Or, it could also be spent on boosting electricity
production once and for all, since most of

00:17:47.259 --> 00:17:51.070
the country is shrouded in darkness at night.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:58.610
But of course, a ski resort or a vacation
town is much more chic.

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:02.370
Anyway, what do you think, do you think that
the country, in general, can benefit from

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:03.970
these tourism projects?

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:08.350
How can they fill these hotels while North
Korea remains such a repressed place, where

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.639
one can’t even move without a guide?

00:18:10.639 --> 00:18:12.320
Leave your answer in the comments.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:15.600
So I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did, and don’t forget to

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:16.659
subscribe for brand new videos.

00:18:16.659 --> 00:18:19.409
Don’t forget to check out our friends at
the Reconsider Media Podcast - they provided

00:18:19.409 --> 00:18:21.760
the vocals in this episode that were not mine.

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:24.970
Also, this channel is possible because of
Patreon, and our patrons on that platform.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:29.590
Please consider joining them and supporting
our mission of providing independent political

00:18:29.590 --> 00:18:30.590
coverage.

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:34.449
And as always, I’ll see you in the next
video.

